commit 40eaa75794bbfa01c9372f10abd48cf19e218dd2
Author: Greg Zuro <greg@zuro.net>
Date:   Mon Jun 8 23:42:54 2026 -0700

    todos: centralize the status token set on TodoStatus::ALL (#236)

    Adding `waiting`/`needs_review` meant editing six hardcoded status lists, which
    is exactly the drift hazard that let the form and filter sets fall out of sync.
    Make panopt-core's `TodoStatus` the single source of truth and derive the rest.

    - core: `TodoStatus::ALL` (canonical ordered list) + `as_str` made `const fn`;
      a test with an exhaustive match guards that every variant is in ALL.
    - panoptd: parse_status builds its "expected ..." error from TodoStatus::ALL.
    - panopt CLI: todo_form STATUSES is now a const derived from TodoStatus::ALL;
      viewer's parse_status_suffix validates via TodoStatus::parse.
    - panopt-zellij-logic: can't depend on core (wasm, dependency-light), so it
      keeps a STATUS_TOKENS const (now the single in-crate copy, used by
      parse_status_suffix). panopt gains a dev-dependency on it purely so a guard
      test (todo_form::tests::status_tokens_match_core) asserts STATUS_TOKENS stays
      equal to core's ALL - drift now fails CI.

    Remaining intentional copies: the tool-surface doc prose (const &str
    descriptions) and the TodoFilter enums (a parallel filter concept, not the
    status list). Adding a status is now: one enum variant (+ as_str/parse, compiler-
    enforced) + ALL + the plugin's STATUS_TOKENS (guard-tested) + colour/filter UX.

    Entire-Checkpoint: 1ccfc838cbbf

